@startuml sequence_frame_recording
title Frame Recording — Trainer → RecordingController → FrameRecorder → frames/{prefix}episode_NNNN.{ext}

actor "Researcher" as R
participant "EATrainer / CMAESTrainer / PSOTrainer /\nCoEvolutionTrainer / AgileRLTrainer /\nNEAT family / QDax" as T
participant "ExperimentLogger" as EL
participant "RecordingController" as RC
participant "UnifiedEvaluator" as UE
participant "FrameRecorder" as FR
participant "PettingZooWrapper\n(render_mode='rgb_array')" as PZ
participant "imageio" as IO
participant "Filesystem\n<run_dir>/frames/" as FS

R -> T: train(config) where\nconfig.recording = RecordingConfig(\n  enabled=True, mode=RecordingMode.COUNT,\n  max_recordings=10, fps=20, fmt='mp4', ...)

== Recording setup (once per train()) ==
T -> RC: RecordingController(config, logger, max_steps, seed)
RC -> EL: get_frame_recorder(... episode_prefix or 'train_')
EL -> FR: FrameRecorder(run_dir/'frames', ...)
FR --> RC: recorder (enabled?)
RC -> UE: UnifiedEvaluator(max_steps, frame_recorder=recorder)
note over RC
  Resolves the cadence schedule from ``RecordingConfig.mode``:
   • COUNT    → max_recordings evenly-spread fraction checkpoints in [0,1]
   • EVERY    → record on every observe()
   • INTERVAL → checkpoints at every_n_steps env-step multiples
   • FINAL    → no mid-run checkpoints
  Disabled controller (recording off / NoOpLogger / imageio missing)
  makes observe()/finalize() cheap no-ops.
end note

== Per-iteration hook (wherever the trainer reports progress) ==
loop each generation / iteration
    T -> T: _on_progress(callback, ProgressEvent(current, total, env_steps, ...), champion)
    T -> RC: observe(event, champion)
    alt event crosses the next checkpoint (per mode)
        RC -> RC: champion()  (lazy — only when due)
        RC -> UE: evaluate(policy | policy_map,\n  iteration=event.current, env_steps=event.env_steps)
        UE -> PZ: reset()
        UE -> FR: start_episode(idx, iteration, env_steps)
        activate FR
        loop step
            UE -> PZ: render() → np.ndarray (H,W,3) uint8
            UE -> FR: add_frame(frame)
            UE -> PZ: step(actions)
        end
        UE -> FR: end_episode()
        FR -> IO: imwrite(frames/train_episode_{idx:04d}.mp4, frames, fps)
        IO -> FS: write artefact
        FR -> FS: append entry to frames/recordings.json (file, iteration, env_steps)
        deactivate FR
    else not due
        RC --> T: (skip — champion() not called)
    end
end

== End of run ==
T -> RC: finalize(champion, iteration, env_steps)
note right of RC
  Always emits one final rollout unless the final checkpoint
  was already captured (deduped by (iteration, env_steps)).
  Covers QDax and the DEAP-internal EA μ±λ strategies whose
  loops can't be hooked mid-run, and guarantees at least one
  artefact on tight budgets.
end note

== Variants ==
note right of T
  • NEAT / HyperNEAT / ES-HyperNEAT: a ``neat.reporting.BaseReporter``
    (``_RecordingReporter``) forwards each generation's champion to
    ``RecordingController.observe``.
  • Co-evolution: the champion provider returns a per-agent
    ``policy_map`` (each side's best policy by role prefix); the
    evaluator dispatches per agent rather than broadcasting one policy.
  • AgileRL: the champion is the live ``AgileRLPolicyWrapper`` (built once,
    reused — weight updates are visible); cadence runs on the env-step axis.
  • QDax: records only via ``finalize`` (JAX-vectorised scoring, no live env).
  The controller reuses the same ``ExperimentLogger`` that writes
  ``metrics.csv`` / ``summary.json`` so ``frames/`` shares one ``run_dir``.
end note
@enduml
